# Do not run dependency lifecycle scripts on install.
#
# This is not paranoia, it is the difference between installing and not
# installing. better-sqlite3 ships a binding.gyp and declares no install script,
# and npm's documented behaviour in that case is to run `node-gyp rebuild`
# itself. node-gyp's configure step then demands Python, make and a C++
# compiler, and fails the whole install before it ever reaches the prebuilt
# binary that better-sqlite3 would have loaded anyway. Verified: with a PATH
# containing no python3, `npm ci` exits 1 on "Could not find any Python
# installation to use"; with this file, it succeeds and the prebuild loads.
#
# It is also the right supply-chain default for a project whose whole security
# story is "one prompt can run anything".
#
# If you add a dependency that genuinely needs its install script, run that one
# explicitly rather than deleting this file.
ignore-scripts=true
